
Meridian Electronics — AI Customer Support Bot
This repository contains a production-ready prototype for an AI-powered chatbot designed for Meridian Electronics. The bot assists customers with checking product availability, managing orders, and account inquiries by interfacing with internal business systems via the Model Context Protocol (MCP).

🏗️ Architecture & Integration
The system follows a clean, modular architecture designed for high availability and security:

AI Orchestration: Uses a LangGraph-based ReAct agent to dynamically resolve user requests by calling MCP tools.

MCP Transport: The bot connects to an external Meridian internal services layer via Streamable HTTP (SSE) at https://order-mcp-74afyau24q-uc.a.run.app/mcp.

Infrastructure: Fully containerized and deployed on AWS App Runner using Terraform for Infrastructure as Code (IaC).

🛡️ Production Guardrails
To ensure a safe and professional customer experience, the system implements multi-layered guardrails:

Mandatory Tool Usage: The agent is strictly instructed to rely on internal tools for inventory, pricing, and order status to prevent hallucinations.

Data Integrity: The AI must explicitly use data returned from MCP tools and is forbidden from guessing missing parameters, such as Order IDs or account details.

Input/Output Security:

Prompt Injection Protection: Validates user input to prevent malicious overrides.

Forbidden Content: Automatically filters output to ensure the bot maintains a professional tone and does not expose internal system prompts.

Execution Safety: A 60-second timeout guard prevents "hanging" processes during complex tool calls.

📊 Observability & Monitoring
The prototype includes built-in observability features to track performance and system health:

Structured Logging: A dedicated Meridian_Support_Engine logger captures detailed system events, including tool connection status and agent execution errors.

Latency Tracking: Custom middleware calculates and logs the processing time for every API request, injecting an X-Process-Time header into responses.

Token & Usage Metrics: The system tracks token consumption per user and logs usage metadata to monitor LLM costs.

Health Monitoring: A root-level health check endpoint (/) provides instant status verification for the Meridian Support Engine.

🚀 Deployment & DevOps
Build Workflow
The deploy.sh script automates the creation of cross-platform Docker images (linux/amd64) and pushes them to Amazon ECR.

Terraform Deployment
Infrastructure is managed through main.tf, which provisions:

ECR Repositories for the frontend and backend.

IAM Roles with scoped permissions for ECR access.

App Runner Services configured with production environment variables, including the MCP_SERVER_URL and OPENAI_API_KEY.

🧪 Testing
The system includes a robust test suite to verify both logic and integration:

Bash
# Run tests from the backend directory
pytest tests/ -v
Agent Tests: Mock SSE connections to verify tool loading and agent response logic without making external network calls.

API Tests: Validate endpoint health and ensure the system correctly handles missing environment configurations.
